TOMS is a footwear and lifestyle brand using business to improve lives.  Since 2006, our community has impacted 100,000,000 lives through supporting the work of non-profit organizations around the world. 

We believe in a future where all people have a chance to thrive, that’s why we are committing 1/3 of our profits to grassroots good, in support of the people working to build a more equitable tomorrow.  Because we believe in a future where all people have a chance to thrive, our support is focused on boosting mental health, increasing access to opportunity, and ending gun violence—all elements we know to be essential for progress to take root. We are not changing the world but we are at the feet of the people who are.  So throw on your TOMS and let’s keep moving forward.

@TOMS

Eximus Education is an award-winning UK social enterprise that, using artificial intelligence, specialises in providing personalised but highly affordable tutoring at-scale nationwide in the UK for ALL subjects and at ALL levels.  

We are a corporate member of the UK Tutors Association (TTA) and have been awarded the "Tutoring Company of the Year" award at UK Enterprise Awards 2023. Eximus Education deploys technology in fulfilling its impact agenda as it firmly believes that it is only through tech solutions that value can be created at-scale at an affordable price. We aim to solve the following three key problems faced by the UK tutoring industry: 

(1) Affordability of tutors - we provide up to 60% cheaper price than the average market rate; 

(2) Reliability of tutors - using professional teachers and not just side-hustlers / university students; 

(3) Availability of tutors - a huge volume of vetted tutors across all subjects including STEM and the Arts.

First Step Trust (FST) is an innovative charity which runs a number of social enterprises, including the SMaRT Garage Services network. FST uses enterprise to provide sustainable work and training opportunities in a commercial environment for people excluded from work because of mental health issues or other disadvantages. 

FST trades with the general public, private companies, charities, other social enterprises and the public sector. We offer professional and competitive services in motor vehicle maintenance, design and print and foodservice.  
FST uses social enterprise as a means of supporting people to make the choices that they feel will help them to overcome social exclusion and improve the quality of their life. We do this by providing: 
- personalised work placements in a commercial enterprise;  
- access to training, qualifications and salaried employment;  
- involvement as a colleague with responsibilities; and opportunities for social interaction with team members, suppliers and customers.

The role of KBOP is to support vulnerable individuals who are homeless or at risk of becoming homeless due to their support needs, including but not limited to individuals who are victims of domestic violence, have mental health illnesses, have long term health conditions, are long term unemployed or are ex-offenders to: 
(i) secure accommodation or support them to stay in an existing tenancy;  
(ii) build their skills so that they can independently sustain their tenancy;  
(iii) improve their physical and mental health and wellbeing, including but not limited to facilitating access to appropriate treatment and other clinical support services; and 
(iv) increase employability and find employment;

[ProgressiveEducation.org](http://ProgressiveEducation.org) is an inspiration hub exploring innovations inside and outside of the school system. It includes: 
- Directory of progressive schools/learning communities; 
- Events; 
- Jobs; 
- Information about alternatives to conventional schooling – Home Education, Montessori, Reggio Emilia, Democratic/Self-Directed Education, Forest School, Small Schools, Waldorf, Online Schools, Hybrid Communities; 
- Campaigns; 
- Initiatives for/by young people; 
- Support for parents/carers; 
- School initiatives to enhance the student experience; 
- How to set up a school; 
- Voices of key education stakeholders. 
Progressive Education is a social enterprise which aims to support and excel the movement for change.  
To join the conversation, please join the "Progressive Education Group" on Facebook. This is a supportive community of 8k parents/carers, teachers, academics, psychologists, researchers and pioneering education innovators. It is a place to ask questions, share inspirations and imagine a new educational paradigm. 
You can follow @ProgEducat on Twitter, Instagram and Facebook.

TCES is a family-run, Social Enterprise with a primary social object, to run inclusive, independent schools & services for the most vulnerable, complex and excluded pupils, with neurodiverse identities including; social, emotional and mental health needs & autistic spectrum conditions, as well as conducting other complementary business & related activities, in each case with a view to having a material positive impact on the whole of society;  

This is a clear social mission in which society profits & at its centre is the inclusion of our pupils. Since inception we have never permanently excluded a single pupil. Our social mission is to employ our graduate pupils within our schools and services creating a virtuous circle. Our integrated services enable our TCES pupils to be the 21st Century Citizens that we can all be proud of.  

We are a social enterprise that is changing the world for the better. That is the TCES way.

